---
// The top of the landing page: what this is, a picture of the panel, and the
// two ways in.
import { appUrl, siteRoot } from '../site/paths'

const GETTING_STARTED =
  'https://github.com/cmdcolin/bender/blob/main/docs/GETTING-STARTED.md'
---

<h1 class="heroHead">Simulated circuit bending</h1>
<p class="pitch">
  A toy keyboard, a drum machine and a small FM chip, wired up in the browser:
  starve the supply until the chip reboots, solder a bend spot, bridge the
  trigger pins, and run the whole thing through tape delay, reverb and
  distortion. You work it from the signal path diagram rather than a wall of
  sliders, and every board it makes is a link you can send.
</p>
<figure class="figure">
  <img
    src={`${siteRoot}panel-callout.jpg`}
    width="1600"
    height="900"
    alt="The panel drawn large on the left and the whole app small beside it, with the panel ringed in red where it sits down the right-hand side of the window: the toy board and its shared supply at the top, the chaos oscillator, noise and sampler feeding the mix bus, the bend slots beside the pedals and the tape machine, and the feedback bus running back under the whole run"
  />
</figure>
<p class="cta">
  <a class="btn primary big" href={appUrl}>
    Open the app →
  </a>
  <a class="btn big" href={GETTING_STARTED}>
    Getting started
  </a>
</p>
